flowchart TB

    subgraph ROW1["PHASE A — DATA UNDERSTANDING AND PREPARATION · Steps 1–3"]
        direction LR

        A["1. Problem Definition<br/>Define the goal of predicting monthly rent with linear regression, adapting the house-price brief to the available rental data"]

        B["2. Data Collection and Inspection<br/>Load the 4,746 rental listings from six cities and check data types, missing values, duplicates, and column meanings"]

        C["3. Exploratory Data Analysis<br/>Study the heavily skewed rent distribution and its links with city, furnishing, size, and bathroom count"]

        A --> B --> C
    end

    subgraph ROW2["PHASE A — DATA UNDERSTANDING AND PREPARATION · Steps 4–6"]
        direction LR

        D["4. Data Cleaning<br/>Parse the Floor text into numeric features, drop weak columns, merge rare categories, and remove 107 implausible outliers"]

        E["5. Feature Selection<br/>Check feature relevance using correlations and median rents, test multicollinearity with VIF, and keep 9 features"]

        F["6. Transformation and Data Split<br/>Log-transform rent, then scale and encode features in a pipeline fitted on the 80% training set only"]

        D --> E --> F
    end

    subgraph ROW3["PHASE B — MODELLING AND EVALUATION · Steps 7–9"]
        direction LR

        G["7. Linear Regression Baseline<br/>Train on log(rent) and compare with a raw-rent model to confirm the benefit of the log transform"]

        H["8. Regularization and Tuning<br/>Tune Ridge, Lasso, and ElasticNet with 5-fold GridSearchCV to test whether penalties reduce overfitting"]

        I["9. Polynomial and Cross-Validation<br/>Test degree-2 terms and check stability across folds, then select the simpler linear model"]

        G --> H --> I
    end

    subgraph ROW4["PHASE B — INTERPRETATION AND REPORTING · Steps 10–12"]
        direction LR

        J["10. Model Evaluation<br/>Assess the 20% test set using MAE, RMSE, MAPE, and R², with residual plots and error by city"]

        K["11. Coefficient Interpretation<br/>Convert coefficients into percentage effects on rent, such as the impact of city, furnishing, and size"]

        L["12. Insights, Reporting, and Repository<br/>Write recommendations, limitations, and the full report, then publish the notebook and report to GitHub"]

        J --> K --> L
    end

    ROW1 --> ROW2
    ROW2 --> ROW3
    ROW3 --> ROW4

    N["Scope Note<br/>Data covers rental listings only; crime rate and transport distance were<br/>unavailable, so rent is the target and results show association, not causation"]

    ROW4 -.-> N

